      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "NOAA Photo Library",
      "description": "Greetings from Texas. \nThe National Weather Service Spaceflight Meteorology Group (SMG) supports NASA human spaceflight operations at Johnson Space Center (JSC) in Houston, Texas. This photo was taken in the Space Shuttle Mission Control Center. SMG provides weather forecasts, briefings, and decision support for the Space Shuttle and International Space Station operations, as well as meteorological consultation support for NASA's next generation of human spaceflight vehicles that will travel to the Space Station, the Moon, and eventually onto Mars. SMG customers include NASA Flight Directors, Flight Controllers, Astronauts, and Mission Management Team. In addition, SMG advises the Johnson Space Center community of adverse weather impacting the JSC complex in Houston.\n\nPictured (from left): Tammi Barreras, Frank Brody, Kurt Van Speybroeck, Richard Lafosse, Doris Hood, Tim Oram, Steve Early, Mark Wiley, Tim Garner, Brian Hoeth.",
